WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.810
Once upon a time, Tom Holland was best known
for starring in the stage version of Billy

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.700
Elliot and the 2012 disaster flick The Impossible.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.380
Of course, that all changed when the British
actor appeared in Captain America: Civil War,

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.720
donning the iconic Spider-Man suit to fight
against Steve Rogers.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.860
"What's up everybody?!"

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:22.120
Marvel fans everywhere thought Holland absolutely
killed it as Peter Parker and they also agreed

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.800
he looked ripped as everybody's favorite web-slinger.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.600
He might've even made some of his co-stars
jealous for how well-liked he was in the flick.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.300
"Listen, Tom's a little a------,alright?

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.800
Tom has his own base camp, he has like an
entourage, he's a lot.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.240
He's a lot to deal with."

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.170
But how did he physically transform from a
scrawny tot into one of the world's most famous

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:43.880
superheroes?

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.240
Here's everything you need to know about how
Tom Holland turned himself into Spider-Man.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.100
Shaking it into shape

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.800
Unlike a certain actor who's best known for
playing Star-Lord, Tom Holland was in great

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.200
shape long before landing the role of Spider-Man.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.690
He started out taking hip-hop dance lessons
in England as a kid and went on to study ballet

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.260
for two years in hopes of landing the title
role in Billy Elliot.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.660
In addition to helping him get bigger, Holland's
dance background has really aided him as an

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.160
actor.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.880
He told Interview Magazine, "I'm very happy
I had that training.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.200
It's been so valuable to my career, and I've
used it on almost everything I've done since."

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.140
That experience certainly came into good use
when he cross-dressed for Lip Sync Battle

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.440
with exactly zero fear of losing any dude
cred.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.100
Hitting the mats

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.620
Every Avenger has his or her particular skillset.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.820
Iron Man flies and blasts stuff.

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:34.340
Black Widow does martial arts.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:39.530
Spider-Man climbs walls, does flips, and makes
Olympic gold medalists look like old men.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.040
Of course, Peter Parker got his acrobatic
skills courtesy of a radioactive spider bite.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.400
Tom Holland, on the other hand, gained his
gymnastic abilities after years of hard work,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.340
dedication, and risking his neck.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.040
Like his dancing history, he credits his stage
work on Billy Elliot with his earliest exposure

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.020
to gymnastics.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.240
"They trained me in gymnastics while I was
during that show and it's just something I

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.720
kept up while finishing the show and for my
auditions for Spider-Man."

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.920
Holland is also into free running, a form
of parkour that emphasizes "creative expression."

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:16.800
In other words, it involves a lot of acrobatics,
not to mention some semi-dangerous stunts.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:21.520
Speaking with Metro, Holland once explained,
"Me and my mates go free running all the time….I've

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.340
probably jumped four meters on to grass and
two meters between buildings."

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.940
In addition to keeping him agile and limber—which
is essential if you're going to play the wall-crawler

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.410
himself—Holland's gymnastic abilities might've
helped him land the role of Spider-Man in

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.200
the first place.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.180
During the audition process, he transformed
what would've been a run-of-the-mill screen

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.780
test into an eye-catching exercise of his
flipping skills.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:47.300
"And I basically did a somersault into frame
and a somersault out of frame; I need them

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.980
to know that I've got some gymnastics abilities
and stuff."

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.260
Considering Tom Holland is the guy currently
wearing the Spidey suit, it looks like his

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.150
acrobatic skills paid off.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.540
"Finally, here we go."

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.160
Changing things up

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.840
Another training technique Tom Holland has
adopted to swell up to Spider-Man size is

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.780
circuit training.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.680
This controversial exercise involves wearing
an elevation mask while performing multiple

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.450
sets of reps, like burpees or bicep curling,
one after another, with almost no rest in

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.420
between stations.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.740
And that's not the only experimental exercise
he's tried; he's also given electronic muscle

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.760
stimulation a whirl along the way, too.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:28.100
"And they put pads on you and you workout
while the pade electrocute you.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.080
And it sucks.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.580
It really really sucks."

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.450
And while he had some trouble with it at first
…

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.770
"I tell you, I did it once and I didn't go
to the toilet for two days."

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:42.140
...He's since given it another go, hopefully
with less troubling consequences.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:43.900
Punching it out

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.820
If you want to be an Avenger, sooner or later
you're going to throw down with some bad guys.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.680
Luckily, Holland is big into combat sports.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.390
Not only is he an MMA fan, showing up at UFC
events, he also spends quite a bit of time

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.880
in the gym, learning all he can about the
sweet science.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:03.240
As a result, Holland totally knows what he's
doing when he pulls on a pair of gloves.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.000
"My mind just got blown.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.160
His might be as well."

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.960
When he's not punishing those punching bags,
Holland also does every other gym activity

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.500
imaginable, including chin-ups, side lateral
raises, and even borrowing Thor's hammer to

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.180
beat on some massive tires.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.590
So, perhaps one of the most effective elements
of his workout regime is how consistently

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.200
he hits the gym, while still mixing up his
routines.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:30.620
"Ah, that was awesome."

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.140
Thanks for watching!

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.870
